# Neural Junkie Environment Configuration
#
# Primary configuration: desktop Settings panel → saved to ~/.neural-junkie/config.json
# Env vars below are optional overrides when set (CI/Makefile).

# Ollama models (used by make agents / load-env.sh; keep in sync with ~/.neural-junkie/config.json)
OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen3.5:9b
OLLAMA_CODE_MODEL=qwen3.5:27b
# Hub-wide concurrent Ollama generations (in-process agents share one semaphore).
# Default in code is 1; make server-regression and release-prep use 2 for collab gates.
# Lower if Ollama becomes unstable; raise only with enough RAM/CPU headroom.
# NJ_OLLAMA_MAX_CONCURRENCY=2
# Collab gate tuning (layer-gate LAYER=collab-core sets these automatically):
# NJ_REGRESSION_SLIM_ROSTER=1      # pause non-core specialists during collab gates
# NJ_REGRESSION_CLAUDE_CLOUD=1     # route @Claude to cloud API (saves Ollama slots)
# NJ_REQUIRE_FULL_BOOT=1           # never SKIP_BOOT during collab layers
# NJ_SCENARIO_PROFILE=core         # @SoftwareArchitect @BackendEngineer @Claude
# Optional second Ollama for isolation (run `OLLAMA_HOST=127.0.0.1:11435 ollama serve`):
# OLLAMA_HOST=127.0.0.1:11435
# Hub async session summaries (dedicated small model; separate from OLLAMA_MODEL / agents)
# NJ_SESSION_SUMMARY_MODEL=qwen2.5:3b
# NJ_SESSION_SUMMARY_TIMEOUT=90s

# Anthropic API Configuration
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_anthropic_api_key_here

# Hugging Face (hosted inference + gated model downloads)
# HF_TOKEN=hf_your_token_here

# Server Configuration
SERVER_PORT=18765
SERVER_HOST=localhost

# Hub memory / heap profiling (local only; binds pprof to loopback)
# NEURAL_JUNKIE_PACKS_CATALOG_URL=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/camronwood/neural-junkie/main/packs/catalog.json
# Domain pack zips: per-pack GitHub release assets (see docs/PACKS.md); catalog-only install requires network.

# NEURAL_JUNKIE_DEBUG=1 enables GET /api/debug/hub-memory and http://127.0.0.1:6060/debug/pprof/
# Dev collab/conversation debugging:
#   make server-debug          # hub + log to /tmp/nj-hub.log
#   make server-log            # tail collab lines (separate terminal)
#   make debug-session         # offline last-session.json
#   make debug-collab COLAB=ec2cdef8 CHANNEL=collab-ec2cdef8-...
#   make debug-messages CHANNEL=dm-camron-assistant TAIL=15
#   make collab-smoke              # in-process API phase test (CI / pre-release)
#   make collab-smoke LIVE=1       # live hub (needs agents for reviewing→executing)
#   make collab-scenario SCENARIO=planning-two-agent   # live agents; PROFILE=fast|realistic
#   make collab-scenario SCENARIO=resource-api-schema-planning  # needs Gemini + PlatformEngineer
#   make collab-scenarios          # all scenarios in scenarios/collab/
#   make collab-scenario-matrix    # sweep profiles and round budgets
# NEURAL_JUNKIE_SCENARIO_REPO=/path/to/Phoenix   # optional workspace for resource-api-schema-planning
# NJ_SCENARIO_ALLOW_FILE_FALLBACK=1            # dev only: allow discussion fallback when hub file-change missing
# Deliverable judge (scenario harness — independent of the agent that produced the file)
# Default: cloud-first (hub @Claude), Ollama fallback when cloud errors (NJ_DELIVERABLE_JUDGE_FALLBACK_OLLAMA=1).
# NJ_DELIVERABLE_JUDGE_PROVIDER=claude          # claude | gemini | cursor | ollama
# NJ_DELIVERABLE_JUDGE_MODE=hub                 # hub | cli | ollama (ollama = local only)
# NJ_DELIVERABLE_JUDGE_MODEL=qwen2.5-coder:14b  # Ollama fallback model
# NJ_DELIVERABLE_JUDGE_FALLBACK_OLLAMA=1        # fall back to Ollama when cloud judge fails
# NJ_DELIVERABLE_JUDGE_MIN_INTERVAL_S=13              # pace Gemini API calls when provider=gemini
# NJ_DELIVERABLE_JUDGE_GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash-lite  # only when provider=gemini
# NJ_DELIVERABLE_JUDGE_AGENT=Claude             # hub agent when provider=claude/cursor/gemini and mode=hub
# NJ_DELIVERABLE_JUDGE_TIMEOUT=180
# NJ_DELIVERABLE_JUDGE_SKIP=1                   # skip LLM judge (regex checks only)
# Desktop workspace context: Auto (default) | Always | Off — localStorage key workspace-context-mode
#   ./scripts/debug-collab.py session --help
# NEURAL_JUNKIE_PPROF_ADDR=127.0.0.1:6060
# Parent directory for collaboration execution sandboxes (<dir>/<collaboration-id>/).
# Default when unset: ~/.neural-junkie/collaborations. Also settable as collaboration.assets_root in config.json or Settings → AI Providers.
# NEURAL_JUNKIE_COLLAB_ASSETS_DIR=~/development/collab-output
# NEURAL_JUNKIE_CAPABILITY_PROFILES=/path/to/model-capability-profiles.json  # override benchmark routing profiles

# NEURAL_JUNKIE_SKIP_SESSION_RESTORE=1  # one boot: skip ~/.neural-junkie/last-session.json (default channels only)
# NEURAL_JUNKIE_FORCE_SESSION_RESTORE=1  # dev only: load last-session.json even when >64MB (may OOM; normally auto-archived)

# MCP tool servers (Backend, DevOps, Database, BiologyExpert, CAD, AWS, Incident, Browser) are configured in
# Settings → AI & providers and ~/.neural-junkie/config.json ("mcp", "hf").
# Domain packs toggle specialist MCP automatically — no ENABLE_*_MCP env vars.
# Default MCP ports include AWS=8092, INCIDENT=8093, and BROWSER=8094 (see internal/mcp/server.go).

# MCP Resource Server Configuration
# Enable MCP resource server for accessing exported agent knowledge
ENABLE_MCP_RESOURCES=true
MCP_RESOURCES_PORT=8086

# MCP Export Storage Configuration
# Directory for storing exported agent knowledge (defaults to ~/.neural-junkie/exports)
MCP_EXPORTS_DIR=~/.neural-junkie/exports

# Claude Code CLI (default deliverable judge + @Claude collab agent)
# Install: npm install -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code
# Auth: claude login  (OAuth, preferred for @Claude)  OR  ANTHROPIC_API_KEY for direct API only
# Hub @Claude strips ANTHROPIC_API_KEY from the CLI subprocess so OAuth wins; keep the key here
# only if other hub features need the Anthropic API. Set NEURAL_JUNKIE_CLAUDE_CUSTOM_ROUTING=1
# to pass ANTHROPIC_API_KEY through to the Claude CLI instead.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_anthropic_api_key_here
# CLAUDE_WORK_DIR=/path/to/your/project

# Gemini CLI (optional — set NJ_DELIVERABLE_JUDGE_PROVIDER=gemini to use as judge)
# Google ended Code Assist OAuth for individuals on 2026-06-18 — use a Gemini API key instead.
# Create at https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey then either:
#   Put one key per line in .gemini-api-key   (gitignored, preferred for local dev)
#   GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here   (in env.local)
# GEMINI_WORK_DIR=/path/to/your/project
# Optional isolated headless auth config (default: scripts/gemini-headless-home in repo)
# NEURAL_JUNKIE_GEMINI_CLI_HOME=/path/to/gemini-headless-home
# Deliverable judge model (separate free-tier quota from chat Flash; used when metadata deliverable_judge=true)
# NJ_DELIVERABLE_JUDGE_GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash-lite

# CLI Agent - Cursor (Optional)
# Enables a Cursor CLI-backed agent in the chat.
# Requires the Cursor CLI to be installed: curl https://cursor.com/install -fsS | bash
# Get API key from your Cursor account settings, then either:
#   echo 'your_key' > .cursor-api-key   (gitignored, preferred for local dev)
#   CURSOR_API_KEY=your_cursor_api_key_here   (in env.local)
CURSOR_WORK_DIR=/path/to/your/project

# Confluence Cloud Configuration (Optional)
# Required for Confluence documentation agents
# Get API token from: https://id.atlassian.com/manage-profile/security/api-tokens
CONFLUENCE_DOMAIN=yourcompany.atlassian.net
CONFLUENCE_EMAIL=your.email@company.com
CONFLUENCE_API_TOKEN=your_confluence_api_token_here

# Google Meet notes (Assistant) — optional env override for OAuth app credentials.
# Prefer Settings → Integrations → Google Meet notes (saved on hub at ~/.neural-junkie/assistant/google_oauth_app.json).
# NEURAL_JUNKIE_GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=your_client_id.apps.googleusercontent.com
# NEURAL_JUNKIE_GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=your_client_secret
# NEURAL_JUNKIE_GOOGLE_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URL=http://localhost:18765/api/assistant/google/callback

# Assistant web search (Settings → Integrations → Web search)
# NEURAL_JUNKIE_WEB_SEARCH_ENABLED=1
# NEURAL_JUNKIE_WEB_SEARCH_PROVIDER=tavily
# NEURAL_JUNKIE_WEB_SEARCH_API_KEY=tvly-...
# NEURAL_JUNKIE_WEB_SEARCH_KEYLESS=1
# Brave (requires API key + card for free credits): NEURAL_JUNKIE_WEB_SEARCH_PROVIDER=brave

# Slack Connect (dev overrides; release builds embed vendor/oauth.json)
# NEURAL_JUNKIE_SLACK_DISABLED=1  # block Socket Mode (make server-regression sets this automatically)
# NEURAL_JUNKIE_SLACK_ENABLED=0   # alias disable when saved config.json has Slack enabled
# NEURAL_JUNKIE_SLACK_CLIENT_ID=your_slack_client_id
# NEURAL_JUNKIE_SLACK_CLIENT_SECRET=your_slack_client_secret
# NEURAL_JUNKIE_SLACK_APP_TOKEN=xapp-your_app_token
# NEURAL_JUNKIE_SLACK_OAUTH_RELAY_BASE=https://nj-slack-oauth-relay.YOUR_SUBDOMAIN.workers.dev
# NEURAL_JUNKIE_SLACK_REDIRECT_URL=https://your-relay.example/api/slack/oauth/callback
# NEURAL_JUNKIE_SLACK_USE_OAUTH_RELAY=1


